WEBVTT

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:05.100
Infinite Ryvius

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:22.550
I commend you all for putting up
with these three tough, long weeks.

00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:27.250
Ryvius is riding Geduld's current
toward Mars at a depth of Sere 4, 590...

00:00:28.030 --> 00:00:31.050
...at a speed of 0.8 herschels.

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:37.560
Once there, rescue will arrive from the
Orbital Security Bureau based on Mars.

00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:40.240
We'll be there soon. Let's hang in there.

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:47.540
<i>We'll be saved shortly.</i>

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:51.180
<i>While telling myself that, I
<i>still felt a sense of anxiety.</i></i>

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:52.810
<i>Maybe it's the air within Ryvius.</i>

00:00:55.150 --> 00:00:56.550
<i>It just felt that way.</i>

00:00:56.650 --> 00:01:01.160
Infinite Ryvius

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:08.030
If you're going to walk, right here will be fine

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:12.040
Although loneliness...

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:16.370
...can sometimes be unbearable

00:01:16.870 --> 00:01:23.610
There's the benefit of not hurting anyone...

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:28.690
...and the benefit of not being exposed...

00:01:28.690 --> 00:01:31.650
...and hurt by others as well

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:39.190
At the opposite side of the frozen sea...

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:42.970
...the dream and the reality...

00:01:42.970 --> 00:01:46.600
...that you saw cross paths

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:50.300
Some light is shed...

00:01:50.970 --> 00:01:54.880
...but how it is done is unknown...

00:01:54.880 --> 00:02:02.110
...so that we can go to a different place

00:02:02.590 --> 00:02:10.120
The things I want have no shape

00:02:10.390 --> 00:02:18.530
Tear the final universe, today until tomorrow

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:32.540
We Didn't Know Anything

00:02:51.970 --> 00:02:53.330
You'd better get some sleep.

00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:59.580
I can't sleep. Besides, if I
continue sending out messages...

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:01.510
...I think it might put the
minds of everyone at ease.

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:03.540
We'll be there in only three days.

00:03:04.750 --> 00:03:06.080
Help will come, right?

00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:07.850
Yes. For sure.

00:03:17.290 --> 00:03:18.260
Are you awake?

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:23.190
Did you hear? Two people
quit Sandy's team.

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:25.460
They lack enough grit.

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:30.330
You know, everything seems to
have changed so much, it's scary.

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:33.470
Are you lonely without Ikumi around?

00:03:36.850 --> 00:03:38.900
I just might be.

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:44.510
The Solid's late! Send me the data!

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:46.650
Vital Guarder, posture control!

00:03:49.690 --> 00:03:51.430
Marco, watch behind you!

00:03:51.430 --> 00:03:53.260
Just because it's a simulation is
no reason to let your guard down.

00:03:53.830 --> 00:03:56.630
Got it. 24, 343, 211.

00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:58.700
Match the body to the surface of Geduld!

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:00.300
We're not gonna make it.

00:04:03.370 --> 00:04:04.360
You're too slow.

00:04:04.870 --> 00:04:06.900
1,020 seconds to target.

00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:09.040
Transferring target to Solid.

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:11.040
442, 92, 221.

00:04:11.510 --> 00:04:12.210
Locked on!

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:16.010
Fire!

00:04:19.790 --> 00:04:21.760
Why do we have to do this so long?

00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:25.120
Is this place the Army?

00:04:27.860 --> 00:04:29.730
You've been quiet lately.

00:04:32.530 --> 00:04:35.160
I'll bet you're beginning to
find operating this interesting.

00:04:36.510 --> 00:04:37.800
I'm just returning a favor.

00:04:38.540 --> 00:04:39.730
Whatever.

00:04:45.610 --> 00:04:47.280
<i>Will rescue really come?</i>

00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:51.080
What are the chances of us
encountering enemies at Mars?

00:04:51.850 --> 00:04:53.220
Forty percent.

00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:55.560
More like sixty percent.

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:58.760
If the submersible ship that
appeared before Ryvius' flight...

00:04:58.760 --> 00:05:01.660
...really did belong to the Orbital
Security Bureau, it would be 80 percent.

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:04.360
What do you intend to do?

00:05:06.070 --> 00:05:10.800
That's why we're creating a Solid and
learning to operate the Vital Guarder.

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:14.400
We're facing professionals.
We alone...

00:05:22.550 --> 00:05:24.610
Stop walking around in that uniform.

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:26.980
Everyone hates the Zwei members.

00:05:27.790 --> 00:05:29.280
All because of you people.

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:39.600
Can we do that?

00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:42.200
We'll just say we couldn't establish
communication because of Geduld.

00:05:42.670 --> 00:05:46.660
As per our initial plan, we'll
proceed at our own discretion.

00:05:55.450 --> 00:05:56.420
Kouji.

00:06:02.660 --> 00:06:03.390
Good morning.

00:06:03.390 --> 00:06:07.800
- Hurry up!
- Hey, don't push!
- How long do we have to wait?

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:10.920
Stay in line! We're
making it, so be quiet!

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:14.230
Hey, what's that weasel doing eating our
food?

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:17.530
Number 34!
Hey, wait!

00:06:17.840 --> 00:06:19.970
We can't handle this with just us five.

00:06:20.210 --> 00:06:22.540
Is it true that all other section
members haven't arrived for their jobs?

00:06:22.540 --> 00:06:24.670
It hardly makes sense
that we should be working.

00:06:25.580 --> 00:06:27.170
The bridge needs fifteen orders!

00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:28.250
What?

00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:32.150
There's no one here.

00:06:32.150 --> 00:06:36.060
What did I tell you! You're about
the only fool working diligently.

00:06:46.900 --> 00:06:51.140
Have any music chips? I'll
trade you anything I have here.

00:06:51.140 --> 00:06:52.540
Really? Give me a moment.

00:06:59.280 --> 00:07:01.080
Hey, you. Won't you come over here?

00:07:01.450 --> 00:07:03.350
Just the girl.

00:07:04.790 --> 00:07:05.490
Let's go.

00:07:05.490 --> 00:07:07.250
You're leaving?

00:07:10.190 --> 00:07:12.420
What do you mean, no uniforms?

00:07:12.560 --> 00:07:14.260
He says Zwei members
stand out too much.

00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:18.400
But we worked so hard to help everyone.

00:07:19.130 --> 00:07:21.670
People now believe we've been
forcing them to do everything.

00:07:21.670 --> 00:07:22.360
Unfortunately.

00:07:23.310 --> 00:07:26.240
What a pity that all that
effort has gone to waste.

00:07:26.980 --> 00:07:28.240
And what are you wearing?

00:07:28.940 --> 00:07:29.910
Cowards.

00:07:44.290 --> 00:07:45.350
Here you go. Fifteen orders.

00:07:46.030 --> 00:07:48.760
You stayed on duty overtime
to prepare this? Thanks.

00:07:49.970 --> 00:07:52.830
I'm sorry to have to leave Rafra
under your care like this.

00:07:55.870 --> 00:07:57.210
Where's Ikumi?

00:07:57.210 --> 00:07:58.970
He's been training on the
Vital Guarder continuously.

00:07:59.940 --> 00:08:01.880
Those guys are even sleeping close by it.

00:08:01.880 --> 00:08:02.940
I see.

00:08:03.380 --> 00:08:04.400
You seem tired.

00:08:05.010 --> 00:08:08.310
The other sections are skipping duties,
so we're stuck doing their work too.

00:08:08.920 --> 00:08:11.510
Please tell everyone to work,
as an order from the bridge!

00:08:12.320 --> 00:08:13.260
S-Sorry...

00:08:13.260 --> 00:08:14.880
Kouji's doing everything he can.

00:08:16.390 --> 00:08:18.760
We'll arrive at Mars in two more
days, so hang on just a bit longer.

00:08:19.960 --> 00:08:21.100
Let's go, Kouji.

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:22.060
Right.

00:08:23.100 --> 00:08:24.070
Bye.

00:08:28.240 --> 00:08:30.030
Did you see how friendly
she's become with him?

00:08:30.510 --> 00:08:32.870
One of his specialties.

00:08:32.870 --> 00:08:35.640
He gradually becomes
friendly with everyone.

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:41.050
Kouji, I'll have beef.

00:08:41.420 --> 00:08:42.380
Sure.

00:08:44.520 --> 00:08:45.990
I'll have beef too.

00:08:45.990 --> 00:08:47.020
Okay.

00:08:47.020 --> 00:08:48.550
I don't want any.

00:08:49.320 --> 00:08:50.830
Thank you.

00:08:50.830 --> 00:08:52.760
I'll have the same, too.

00:08:56.360 --> 00:08:57.800
You don't get any.

00:08:58.030 --> 00:08:58.830
Why not?

00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:01.470
Because you're not working.

00:09:01.470 --> 00:09:04.300
You're the ones who decided to
reward people by their skills, right?

00:09:05.070 --> 00:09:08.630
Given our present situation, that would
in fact be the most rational option.

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:10.340
You heard him.

00:09:10.610 --> 00:09:13.310
B-B-But I'm a Zwei member!

00:09:13.480 --> 00:09:14.810
So what?

00:09:15.380 --> 00:09:18.050
N-No. I just wanted to make
sure you understand that.

00:09:18.620 --> 00:09:19.880
Yes. As long as you understand.

00:09:21.820 --> 00:09:24.020
Kouji, can I have beef?

00:09:25.190 --> 00:09:26.160
Sure.

00:09:27.100 --> 00:09:31.590
K-Kouji! I insist that you refrain from
doing anything to corrupt public morals!

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:33.600
I have no intention of that, Charlie.

00:09:33.940 --> 00:09:34.370
Cha...!

00:09:35.870 --> 00:09:38.770
Only Blue and his guys are
allowed to call me Charlie!

00:09:39.270 --> 00:09:42.000
To you, I'm Good Turtleland the Third!

00:09:42.340 --> 00:09:44.380
What? Charlie isn't your real name?

00:09:44.380 --> 00:09:45.370
What?!

00:09:56.730 --> 00:09:58.590
Juli. What's with that outfit?

00:09:59.760 --> 00:10:00.630
Is anything wrong?

00:10:05.300 --> 00:10:07.060
Things are beginning to take shape.

00:10:07.400 --> 00:10:09.030
Pretty good. I'm impressed.

00:10:09.700 --> 00:10:13.230
Not all Zwei members are idiots. Some
of us have thought things through.

00:10:18.950 --> 00:10:23.320
However, the Solid created by
Kreis alone is not swift enough.

00:10:23.820 --> 00:10:26.150
We need the manpower
to create a Sub-Solid!

00:10:26.150 --> 00:10:27.120
How many people do you need?

00:10:27.120 --> 00:10:30.520
At least twenty. I believe they
can help from the sub-room.

00:10:30.830 --> 00:10:32.920
H-Hey! I'll do it! I'll do it!

00:10:33.260 --> 00:10:34.390
Hey kid, shut up!

00:10:35.800 --> 00:10:38.630
I'm not a kid! And I know
how to do conversions.

00:10:39.230 --> 00:10:41.790
I was the one who found the
robot in the first place!

00:10:41.940 --> 00:10:44.740
Blast you! Who said you
could add such a function?

00:10:45.140 --> 00:10:46.630
Hey, fatso, do something about him!

00:10:46.940 --> 00:10:50.640
H-He doesn't mean any harm. No harm.

00:10:53.820 --> 00:10:54.710
He's here!

00:10:59.090 --> 00:11:00.650
But he's asleep.

00:11:06.700 --> 00:11:09.320
Temperature around the outer wall
of the bow is quickly decreasing!

00:11:10.930 --> 00:11:12.300
Really? Are we through?

00:11:15.870 --> 00:11:18.340
Yes. This sudden change in temperature
is proof that we have arrived...

00:11:18.340 --> 00:11:19.810
...at the Van Allen Belt of Mars.

00:11:20.310 --> 00:11:22.900
Switch all systems to normal navigation.

00:11:23.180 --> 00:11:24.040
Already done.

00:11:25.250 --> 00:11:26.610
Switching over in three minutes.

00:11:29.480 --> 00:11:30.250
It's Mars!

00:11:30.520 --> 00:11:32.110
We made it through the Geduld!

00:11:32.320 --> 00:11:33.310
Great!

00:11:33.590 --> 00:11:34.380
Mars?

00:11:34.520 --> 00:11:35.110
That's right.

00:11:36.120 --> 00:11:39.120
That is the red planet that will save us.

00:11:43.530 --> 00:11:46.020
I'm loading the Solid Program to
take us to satellite orbit.

00:11:46.640 --> 00:11:49.240
Kouji, that's Mars! You hear? Mars!

00:11:49.240 --> 00:11:50.860
I know. I can see it.

00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:53.410
Be happy, Kouji!

00:11:53.410 --> 00:11:54.710
I <i>am</i> happy.

00:11:54.710 --> 00:11:57.640
Okay, make an announcement over
the PA system to let everyone know!

00:11:58.280 --> 00:12:00.580
There'll be no need for that!

00:12:00.580 --> 00:12:01.550
Why not?

00:12:08.560 --> 00:12:10.320
Infinite Ryvius

00:12:13.430 --> 00:12:14.790
Infinite Ryvius

00:12:20.670 --> 00:12:21.840
I have something on the radar!

00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:22.940
A ship?

00:12:22.940 --> 00:12:23.770
Rescuers?

00:12:23.770 --> 00:12:25.100
But there are too many of them.

00:12:25.410 --> 00:12:27.600
They must <i>really</i> be welcoming us.

00:12:28.110 --> 00:12:28.800
It's an ambush.

00:12:30.710 --> 00:12:32.200
He said it's an ambush!

00:12:32.880 --> 00:12:34.140
Not rescuers?

00:12:48.830 --> 00:12:50.230
The Geduld is affecting our radar!

00:12:50.230 --> 00:12:50.970
They're coming!

00:12:50.970 --> 00:12:52.560
Who's coming?

00:12:52.930 --> 00:12:54.960
You fool. Enemies, obviously.

00:13:07.920 --> 00:13:10.350
Commencing condition Vecker, plan FW.

00:13:10.990 --> 00:13:14.150
Upon initial contact, confirm
target's attacking abilities.

00:13:14.560 --> 00:13:16.820
Battle? With this ship?

00:13:17.330 --> 00:13:18.530
That's right.

00:13:18.530 --> 00:13:19.760
That's crazy!

00:13:19.760 --> 00:13:21.760
We'll do it even if it is crazy!

00:13:21.760 --> 00:13:24.130
They destroyed the Van Allen
Belt strengthening system...

00:13:24.130 --> 00:13:25.460
...and killed our communication system.

00:13:25.770 --> 00:13:27.500
Those guys are seriously
trying to destroy us!

00:13:28.500 --> 00:13:31.370
Battle? This is pretty heavy stuff.

00:13:31.810 --> 00:13:33.670
But they're here to rescue us, right?

00:13:35.880 --> 00:13:36.970
Prepare for battle.

00:13:38.450 --> 00:13:39.070
Battle...!

00:13:39.950 --> 00:13:42.420
Don't just stand there.
Switch over the system.

00:13:42.820 --> 00:13:43.650
But...!

00:13:43.650 --> 00:13:45.050
Hurry up!

00:13:45.420 --> 00:13:46.680
Wait a minute!

00:13:47.290 --> 00:13:49.590
Don't make decisions based
on suppositions alone.

00:13:49.590 --> 00:13:51.650
The strengthening system could have
broken down for some other reason.

00:13:52.230 --> 00:13:53.690
Do you seriously think so?

00:13:54.060 --> 00:13:57.430
Yes I do. Because there still is a chance
that those are rescue ships out there!

00:13:57.870 --> 00:13:59.360
If you're gonna dream, do it in your sleep.

00:13:59.800 --> 00:14:00.630
But...!

00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:04.300
But, if we fought, we wouldn't
be able to land on Mars.

00:14:05.110 --> 00:14:05.910
Should that happen...

00:14:05.910 --> 00:14:07.810
We won't be able to land anyway!

00:14:14.450 --> 00:14:17.380
I suggest we return into
the Geduld one more time!

00:14:17.720 --> 00:14:21.050
They're likely to come toward
us using the satellite orbit.

00:14:21.260 --> 00:14:22.220
Wait!

00:14:22.590 --> 00:14:25.420
Let's at least try to call for help
with our communication device.

00:14:25.890 --> 00:14:28.020
That'll only give them our position.

00:14:28.160 --> 00:14:29.930
As I said, I have a suggestion!

00:14:30.570 --> 00:14:32.570
We'll calculate the
enemy's estimated course...

00:14:32.570 --> 00:14:34.700
...with records from our
radar, and attack first.

00:14:34.700 --> 00:14:36.570
Do you want to battle that badly?

00:14:36.570 --> 00:14:38.640
It's better than waiting to be destroyed.

00:14:38.640 --> 00:14:41.340
What are you saying? We
have a way out of this!

00:14:41.940 --> 00:14:43.610
I'm sure there's a way!

00:14:43.610 --> 00:14:45.010
Then get us outta this jam now.

00:14:49.280 --> 00:14:52.850
Kouji. Send a message to all
terminals. We're going into battle.

00:14:56.060 --> 00:14:56.790
Hurry!

00:14:56.790 --> 00:14:57.730
No!

00:14:57.730 --> 00:14:58.690
Kouji!

00:15:09.800 --> 00:15:10.770
You know...!

00:15:10.940 --> 00:15:12.100
Let's say the others <i>are</i> enemies.

00:15:12.640 --> 00:15:14.370
How do you suppose
they'll attack this ship?

00:15:15.280 --> 00:15:16.610
Stop talking nonsense!

00:15:16.610 --> 00:15:20.140
Likely a direct attack in the same direction
as the gravity generated by Ryvius.

00:15:20.720 --> 00:15:25.240
It's likely they'll want to get closer to us
to increase the accuracy of their attack.

00:15:26.450 --> 00:15:29.320
If so, we can wait until the very last
moment to see how they'll attack.

00:15:29.990 --> 00:15:32.890
It may be a very slight possibility,
but I think it's worth a shot.

00:15:33.630 --> 00:15:36.360
We don't wanna fight.
We want to be rescued.

00:15:37.070 --> 00:15:39.160
Umm... and my suggestion?

00:15:39.530 --> 00:15:41.470
We haven't got time, you fool!

00:15:42.270 --> 00:15:44.360
Kouji! What would you
do if we were attacked?

00:15:45.270 --> 00:15:47.640
Should that happen, we'd
have no choice but to fight.

00:15:49.010 --> 00:15:52.670
I agree with Kouji. It's our
best chance to survive. Right?

00:15:58.090 --> 00:16:03.220
Okay, we'll go with that. Kouji,
we won't announce this over the PA!

00:16:03.690 --> 00:16:05.560
Send a message to all
terminals! Gently, but clearly!

00:16:06.190 --> 00:16:07.160
Sure thing.

00:16:08.500 --> 00:16:09.760
What did you really want to do?

00:16:10.900 --> 00:16:14.340
If I had a choice, I'd run
away. This is absolutely crazy.

00:16:14.640 --> 00:16:17.440
Ryu. Take a few guys
and block the entrance.

00:16:17.440 --> 00:16:18.340
Gotcha!

00:16:18.340 --> 00:16:19.870
You guys, come with me!

00:16:19.870 --> 00:16:21.440
Is he serious?

00:16:21.440 --> 00:16:22.410
Now!

00:16:24.050 --> 00:16:26.610
Charlie, gather members
to create the Sub-Solid!

00:16:26.610 --> 00:16:28.240
Prepare Vital Guarder for take off.

00:16:29.420 --> 00:16:31.990
Strike back? Are you asking us to battle?

00:16:31.990 --> 00:16:35.010
To contain them. What do you think
we've been practicing for all this time?

00:16:35.390 --> 00:16:37.460
Hell of a time for you
to be getting cold feet.

00:16:37.460 --> 00:16:41.230
Do you have any idea what this means?
If we go to battle, people will die!

00:16:41.230 --> 00:16:43.360
If you don't wanna do
it, why don't you quit?

00:16:43.360 --> 00:16:45.330
They've got hostages, right?

00:16:45.970 --> 00:16:47.970
You have the nerve to give me a
lecture and then back down yourself.

00:16:47.970 --> 00:16:50.700
It would serve you right to not
do anything and get wiped out.

00:16:51.110 --> 00:16:52.410
Bastard!

00:16:52.410 --> 00:16:54.110
The result's the same
no matter how you cut it.

00:16:54.110 --> 00:16:56.130
Either they die, or we die.

00:16:58.810 --> 00:17:01.080
I'm gonna fight this battle, naturally.

00:17:05.350 --> 00:17:07.250
Me, get on that robot?

00:17:07.790 --> 00:17:12.190
What? Me to the sub room too?
I'd rather operate that thing!

00:17:12.290 --> 00:17:14.260
Hey, I hear the enemy's attacking again.

00:17:14.260 --> 00:17:16.430
If they're gonna fight,
what are we to do?

00:17:16.430 --> 00:17:18.470
Aren't the folks on Mars
coming to rescue us?

00:17:18.470 --> 00:17:20.090
We'd better evacuate!

00:17:20.340 --> 00:17:21.320
Evacuate? Where?

00:17:21.570 --> 00:17:24.170
There's no need to rush things.

00:17:24.170 --> 00:17:28.980
I remember them saying on TV once,
that battles in outer space take time...

00:17:28.980 --> 00:17:30.880
...and the act itself is totally meaningless.

00:17:30.880 --> 00:17:32.350
Can't they inform us properly?

00:17:32.350 --> 00:17:34.340
What are they doing? Those fools.

00:17:34.780 --> 00:17:36.310
Give us the details!

00:17:36.420 --> 00:17:39.220
I'm from Deimos! Let me
communicate with my Dad!

00:17:39.590 --> 00:17:41.690
Hold on one moment.

00:17:41.690 --> 00:17:43.050
We'll explain later.

00:17:43.630 --> 00:17:46.190
Aren't you guys doing
things on your own again?

00:17:50.300 --> 00:17:54.360
Stop whining. We're in a
crisis here! Keep quiet!

00:17:57.170 --> 00:17:58.830
We're now in the Mars satellite orbit.

00:17:59.040 --> 00:18:01.010
Outer wall temperature slowly decreasing.

00:18:01.540 --> 00:18:03.270
Gravitational field
developing on starboard.

00:18:07.920 --> 00:18:10.210
Radar recovered! They're approaching.

00:18:10.390 --> 00:18:12.010
Communication's recovered as well!

00:18:14.460 --> 00:18:16.150
Contacting approaching spaceships.

00:18:17.360 --> 00:18:19.350
Can you hear me? This is Ryvius calling.

00:18:19.990 --> 00:18:22.590
Our spaceship has just passed through
the Geduld to arrive in Mars' vicinity.

00:18:22.860 --> 00:18:23.830
It's useless!

00:18:24.800 --> 00:18:28.800
Please listen. On board Ryvius
are 487 students who escaped...

00:18:28.800 --> 00:18:32.640
...from the Astronaut
Training Center Liebe Delta.

00:18:33.140 --> 00:18:35.800
We request to be rescued.
Please open your communication lines.

00:18:36.480 --> 00:18:37.780
This is Ryvius calling.

00:18:37.780 --> 00:18:40.440
Our spaceship has just passed through
the Geduld to arrive in Mars' vicinity.

00:18:41.050 --> 00:18:42.880
We have no intentions of fighting.

00:18:43.420 --> 00:18:44.650
We request to be rescued.

00:18:45.420 --> 00:18:48.050
This is Ryvius. Our spaceship has
just passed through the Geduld...

00:18:48.560 --> 00:18:50.420
...to arrive in Mars' vicinity.

00:18:51.130 --> 00:18:52.090
Please.

00:18:52.660 --> 00:18:53.990
30 seconds to contact.

00:18:54.130 --> 00:18:55.600
Their speed has not changed.

00:18:56.760 --> 00:18:58.890
Please rescue us.

00:19:03.370 --> 00:19:06.600
Please! Please rescue us...

00:19:09.580 --> 00:19:10.540
Juli!

00:19:12.950 --> 00:19:14.380
You're giving up too easily!

00:19:15.520 --> 00:19:16.950
We have evacuated here.

00:19:17.490 --> 00:19:19.220
We have no intentions to fight.

00:19:19.220 --> 00:19:20.690
We just want to be rescued!

00:19:21.220 --> 00:19:22.480
We need help!

00:19:22.890 --> 00:19:23.860
Please!

00:19:23.990 --> 00:19:25.720
Don't fire, please.

00:19:26.190 --> 00:19:31.060
PLEASE DON'T FIRE!!

00:19:37.000 --> 00:19:38.270
Damage is minimal!

00:19:38.640 --> 00:19:41.010
What did I tell ya! They <i>are</i> enemies!

00:19:41.440 --> 00:19:42.880
Develop field on portside!

00:19:43.380 --> 00:19:44.810
Another fleet is approaching!

00:19:45.050 --> 00:19:46.880
Ship type, unknown!

00:19:46.880 --> 00:19:48.480
Switch system over to me!

00:19:48.480 --> 00:19:49.180
Charlie!

00:19:49.420 --> 00:19:50.850
B-But I...

00:19:51.150 --> 00:19:51.880
Hurry up!

00:19:51.950 --> 00:19:53.480
But, you see...!

00:19:56.960 --> 00:19:58.320
The locks to our fire control...!

00:19:58.530 --> 00:19:58.920
What?

00:19:59.390 --> 00:20:00.490
I... I...

00:20:00.830 --> 00:20:01.590
Charlie!

00:20:01.900 --> 00:20:03.020
Don't do it, Charlie!

00:20:03.430 --> 00:20:04.490
Do it, Charlie!

00:20:04.770 --> 00:20:05.700
Charlie!!

00:20:05.770 --> 00:20:06.770
Charlie!!

00:20:06.770 --> 00:20:10.570
SHUT UP! Stop calling me Charlie!

00:20:23.180 --> 00:20:25.150
Our target has fired its main cannon.

00:20:25.450 --> 00:20:26.820
From directly ahead?

00:20:26.820 --> 00:20:28.220
Are they amateurs?

00:20:32.290 --> 00:20:34.320
A portion of their fleet is changing course.

00:20:34.930 --> 00:20:35.930
Did we hit 'em?

00:20:35.930 --> 00:20:36.790
Way to go, Blue.

00:20:37.670 --> 00:20:38.370
I... I...

00:20:38.370 --> 00:20:39.800
Good job, Charlie.

00:20:40.230 --> 00:20:41.430
What have you done?

00:20:42.040 --> 00:20:46.200
We haven't sunk them by any means.
If only they would retreat now.

00:20:46.770 --> 00:20:49.400
Where do you get the nerve for
that damn wishful thinking?

00:20:51.250 --> 00:20:52.970
Fragments of shells fired are returning...

00:20:53.450 --> 00:20:55.880
...so we should spread our field
to the whole area ahead.

00:20:58.390 --> 00:21:03.260
I was mistaken to have left you in
charge. Leave the bridge at once!

00:21:03.590 --> 00:21:04.850
Don't give me orders.

00:21:05.560 --> 00:21:07.220
How long before we make
contact with them again?

00:21:07.700 --> 00:21:09.190
5 hours and 47 minutes.

00:21:11.800 --> 00:21:13.430
I don't want to sit back
and let them attack us.

00:21:13.870 --> 00:21:15.630
Send out the Vital Guarder!

00:21:22.240 --> 00:21:24.400
Target is proceeding in satellite orbit.

00:21:25.110 --> 00:21:27.010
Slight damage to Els 1 and Els 2.

00:21:27.580 --> 00:21:29.050
Sending out a ship to retrieve them.

00:21:29.550 --> 00:21:31.920
Send orbit data of target to Wells Ring.

00:21:32.350 --> 00:21:33.490
Roger.

00:21:33.490 --> 00:21:34.760
Shall we send images as well?

00:21:34.760 --> 00:21:36.120
Show me.

00:21:39.560 --> 00:21:40.750
Hm? The shape's different.

00:21:41.200 --> 00:21:42.750
I'll zoom out.

00:21:45.970 --> 00:21:47.590
What's that?

00:21:52.240 --> 00:21:55.640
<i>I had no idea what was about to happen...</i>

00:21:57.410 --> 00:21:59.810
<i>...nor did I know what power</i>
<i>the Vital Guarder possessed.</i>

00:22:01.220 --> 00:22:02.340
<i>I did not know.</i>

00:22:03.280 --> 00:22:06.280
<i>In fact, we didn't know anything.</i>

00:22:07.940 --> 00:22:12.210
In your dry eyes...

00:22:12.210 --> 00:22:17.290
...a silhouette appears

00:22:17.290 --> 00:22:21.990
The blue colored future...

00:22:21.990 --> 00:22:28.090
...swayed and glittered

00:22:29.900 --> 00:22:38.140
Ah... No one wants...

00:22:38.140 --> 00:22:46.750
...freedom out of pity

00:22:46.750 --> 00:22:55.190
Ah... To the days I feared...

00:22:55.190 --> 00:22:59.090
...that I'd end up hurting someone,

00:22:59.090 --> 00:23:05.460
goodbye

00:23:09.290 --> 00:23:10.820
Infinite Ryvius

00:23:10.820 --> 00:23:12.290
Infinite Ryvius
Next episode: Vital Guarder

00:23:12.290 --> 00:23:12.790
Next episode: Vital Guarder

00:23:12.790 --> 00:23:17.060
Next episode: Vital Guarder
Is the gravity warping power released by
Vital Guarder, sent out from Ryvius...

00:23:17.060 --> 00:23:19.300
Next episode: Vital Guarder
...meant to open a path to our future...

00:23:19.300 --> 00:23:23.170
Next episode: Vital Guarder
...or is it meant to twist our fate?

00:23:23.170 --> 00:23:25.300
Next episode: Vital Guarder
However, right now...

00:23:25.300 --> 00:23:27.270
Next episode: Vital Guarder
...it's the best we
can do just to stay alive...

00:23:27.270 --> 00:23:28.310
Next episode: Vital Guarder
...to survive...!

00:23:28.310 --> 00:23:29.140
Next episode: Vital Guarder
